Design payment gateway
An online platform that securely captures user payment details and orchestrates transactions between
merchants and financial processors.

merchant -> amazon , flipkart , any shop 
payment gateway , payment processor -> stripe

stripe as payment gateway : securely collects payment details and routes payment requests.
stripe as a payment processor : facilitates transactions between merchants and the relevant banking
                                and payment networks.

payment gateway :-
a payment gateway is the platform that collects payment details from users , secures and
tokenizes them , orchestrates the transaction flow , and communiates with the payment
processor.
gateway = "traffic controller of payments"

orchestration -> coordinating all the components involved in completing a payment.

payment processor :-
a payment processor is the financial network entity that actually talks to banks and 
card networks to authorize , capture , and settle the money.
processor = "the system that actually moves the money"


1
gathering of the functional requirements

-> payment intent creation :
   create a payment request containing the order amount and other relevant details.
   
-> checkout session creation
   generate a temporary , secure checkout session for the user.

-> secure card handling
   protect sensitive card information using tokenization and appropriate security controls

-> payment status tracking
   inform the merchant whether a payment succeeded or failed.

the payment card industry data security standard (PCI DSS) is the global security
standard for all entities that sotre , process or transmit cardholder data and/or
sensitive authentication data.

  
4 requirements :-
-> client should be able to initiate payment requests
-> gateway creates a temporary session for the user to enter card details
-> secure PCI-DSS compliance for card data handling
-> transaction status tracking

out of the scope :- Partial payments , returns and refunds

non-functional requirements :-
-> scale :- 10k TPS (transactions per second)
-> CAP : availability << consistency (strong consistency for payment transactions)
-> latency < 200ms response time for payment authorization
-> security : end-to-end encryption , PCI-DSS Level 1 compliance

